lit_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"பாசிலை","parts":[{"text":"பாசிலை","lemma":"பாசிலை","gloss":"green-leaved"}],"gloss":"green-leaved","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முல்லை","parts":[{"text":"முல்லை","lemma":"முல்லை","gloss":"jasmine"}],"gloss":"jasmine"},{"surface":"முகைக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"முகைக்கும்","lemma":"முகைக்கும்","gloss":"will bud"}],"gloss":"will bud","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆய்","parts":[{"text":"ஆய்","lemma":"ஆய்","gloss":"select/beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"தொடி","parts":[{"text":"தொடி","lemma":"தொடி","gloss":"bangle"}],"gloss":"bangles"},{"surface":"அரிவையர்","parts":[{"text":"அரிவை","lemma":"அரிவை","gloss":"young woman"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"அர்","gloss":"pl"}],"gloss":"of the young women"},{"surface":"தந்தை","parts":[{"text":"தந்தை","lemma":"தந்தை","gloss":"father"}],"gloss":"father's"},{"surface":"நாடே","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"country"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"country indeed"}]}],"literal":"Even if the black planet smolders, even if a comet appears / Even if Venus travels towards the southern direction / To fill the inside of the fields, flowers of the bushes to blossom / In the front yard of the house, having given birth to a calf, with gentle eyes / The wild cow's long herd feeds fully on the good grass / With the uprightness of the sceptre, noble people having multiplied / It is indeed the dry land that knows no failure of rain / Resembling the sharp teeth of the young wildcat / Where the green-leaved jasmine will bud / Indeed, it is the country of the father of the young women with beautiful bangles.","translation":"Even if Saturn smolders, even if a comet appears, and even if Venus travels to the southern sky, the rain never fails in this dry land. The fields are filled, bush-flowers blossom, and in the front yards of houses, gentle-eyed wild cows that have just given birth feed on lush, good grass with their long herds. Under a righteous sceptre, noble people multiply. In this land, the green-leaved jasmine buds, resembling the sharp teeth of a wildcat's kitten. Such is the country of the father of these young women with beautiful bangles.","modern":"சனி கிரகம் புகைந்தாலும், தூமகேது தோன்றினாலும், வெள்ளி கிரகம் தெற்கு திசையில் ஓடினாலும், மழை பொய்க்காமல் பெய்யும் புன்புல நாடு அது. வயல்வெளிகள் நிறையுமாறு புதர்களில் மலர்கள் மலர, வீட்டின் முற்றத்தில் கன்றை ஈன்ற சாதுவான கண்களைக் கொண்ட காட்டுப் பசுக்கள் தம்முடைய நீண்ட கூட்டத்தோடு நல்ல புல்லை வயிறார மேயும். செங்கோல் முறைமையால் சான்றோர்கள் பெருகி வாழும் நாடு அது. காட்டுப் பூனைக் குட்டியின் கூர்மையான பற்களைப் போலப் பசிய இலைகளைக் கொண்ட முல்லை அரும்புகள் மலரும். இத்தகைய வளமிக்க நாடு, அழகிய வளையல்களை அணிந்த பெண்களின் தந்தையாகிய பாரியின் நாடாகும்.","explanation":"This poem is a hand-wringing lament (கையறுநிலை) sung by the great poet Kapilar after the death of his beloved patron and friend, Vēḷ Pāri. Kapilar describes the extraordinary fertility and righteousness of Pāri's country, Parampu Nāṭu. Even when astrological portents like the smoldering of Saturn, the appearance of comets, or the southward movement of Venus threaten drought, Pāri's land never suffers from a lack of rain because of his righteous rule. The imagery of wild cows feeding peacefully with their calves in house yards and the delicate jasmine buds resembling the sharp teeth of a wildcat kitten highlight the natural harmony and safety of the land. Now that Pāri is gone, his daughters (the young women with beautiful bangles) are left fatherless, and the poet looks back with deep grief at the glorious country that once was.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}